{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"HeadwireMacHost runs the helper’s host. It listens for paired devices on the USB cable, the network and Direct wireless over TLS with both keys pinned, captures a display with ScreenCaptureKit, encodes it with a low-latency HEVC encoder, sends the frames and the Mac’s sound to each device, and posts the input each device sends back as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CGEvent"},{"type":"text","text":"s. It also runs the pairing window, keeps the trust list and the helper’s key in the keychain, draws the calibration strip a device asks for, and reads the iPad’s source mode request over the Bluetooth link the Mac already holds for HID. It does not decide what a person sees: the menu’s switches, the permissions, the build and the capture display’s mode are resolved by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HeadwireMacKit"},{"type":"text","text":"’s value types, and the menu itself belongs to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HeadwireMac"},{"type":"text","text":" app. The wire formats come from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HeadwireWire"},{"type":"text","text":" and the input events from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HeadwireInput"},{"type":"text","text":", so both ends share one implementation. Much of the streaming and input code is derived from "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/Saffsanity\/sill"},{"type":"text","text":", under the Apache License 2.0."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The virtual display, Sidecar and the private Bluetooth pairing agent are compiled only into the Direct build and are not documented here."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/SessionLifecycle"],"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Headwire